ve  crazy good performance  but i'm also expecting a replacement for  the regular apple tv hd  since there are two models that are  rumored and to make it even more  interesting  there were reports back in 2018 that  apple would be releasing a low-cost  apple tv dongle which would be meant for  those who just want to watch tv content  and this would totally make sense if  apple has a gaming focused high-end  apple tv for those who want to do some  gaming as well  the only problem is that we did recently  get a report saying that the new apple  tv  isn't coming until the end of the year  but i personally don't think that's  gonna happen  because we've been seeing so many leaks  and rumors recently  pointing to a release date much sooner  than that and now  with all of that apple tv stuff out of  the way let's move into the absolute  start of the show  and that's going to be the release of  the brand new 2021 ipad pro  we've been seeing rumors about a new  ipad pro for almost a full year  when ming chico said that apple was  working on a mini led  ipad pro and of course because of the  pandemic we saw many reports saying that  it's going to be delayed until  2021 and quo once again confirmed  that we will in fact be getting a mini  led display  and then et news took it even further  saying that it's going to launch in the  first quarter of 2021  and the same rumor came from digi times  as well  which would mean that the new ipad pro  would have to be released  before the end of march so i'm basically  100  sure that it's going to be released at  apple's march event if they have it  or if not then it's going to be an  online launch my only concern  is that the 11 inch model is going to  get discontinued but both fudge  and love to dream on twitter pointing to  there still being  two models and recently leaked cad  images were leaked  with both 11 inch and 12.9 inch sizes so  that seems much more likely to have both  one thing i am confident about is the  specs  it's going to get a mini led display and  it'll also come with the a14x chip  which is going to be extremely similar  to apple's m1 mac chip  except that it's not going to have all  of the other mac specific hardware  all i know is that it's going to be  extremely powerful  and it most likely is not going to come  with the new design since it just  recently got redesigned  and it seems like apple wants to stick  with the same modern flat side design  for a while  and i personally think that the price  tag is going to be staying basically the  same  eight hundred dollars for the 11 inch if  it does come out and a thousand dollars  for the 12.9 inch  so i'm personally very excited to see  what apple has in store for the next  ipad  pro but we are also expecting one more  ipad  next month and that's the ipad mini i'm  almost 100  sure that it's coming because it's the  only ipad that hasn't been updated  and basically two full years every other  ipad was updated last year  so we should be seeing a new ipad mini  next month  and we have some leaks and rumors to  support that way back in may of 2020  ming chi quo said that we should be  expecting two new ipads  a 10.8 inch ipad in the second half of  2020  and an 8.5 to 9 inch ipad mini  in the first half of 2021. that 10.8  inch ipad turned out to be the ipad air  4  which received a full redesign with the  new rounded corner display  flat sides and back finally a usb c port  and a new touch id power button but we  still haven't seen the mini  so i think it's gonna come next month  because even digitimes said we should be  expecting it to come  alongside the new mini led ipad pro  in the first half of 2021. the main  takeaway is the display size  which should be at least eight inches  potentially up to nine inches  which means that it's almost certainly  getting a full redesign  with a rounded corner display just like  the ipad air 4. we should also be  expecting it to get the same flat sides  and back  as well as the same exa